{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1565073-werewolf-the-essentials","id":1565073,"title":"Werewolf the Essentials","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-11-01T07:27:27-08:00","id":1565073,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Werewolf the Essentials","content":"<i>The Garou have intricate and multi-layered cultures from their written language to their oral histories, the way they dress, and the ways they manifest across editions were presented with very little overlap when it comes to the multiple facets across their society, leading to a rich history and complex societies for Storytellers to weave chronicles together for their troupes.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Book One is the first in a series of Storytellers References meant to offer a modernized lore, cross-edition translation, and robust Storytelling tools to run an inclusive Werewolf tabletop in the 2020s. Contributed to by several renowned World of Darkness authors, and a team of dedicated lifelong fans of the game, we have come together to present you the Werewolf game it was always meant to be. This book contains a lore and cultural roadmap for any new Storyteller looking to delve into the game who finds themselves intimidated by its labyrinthian lore and outdated, problematic story elements.</i><br /> <br /> <i>We monsters ask nothing of you\u2014other than to join</i> us<b>.</b><br /> <br /> After literal years of work, the multi-edition WtA resource book is out!<br /> <br /> Find it on Drivethru!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":25411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","user":"Trav